From b83c0f2402ca839f580147057708adc02598ebaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:05:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10577/11362] Restore 78 acknowledgements I destroyed in
 dac8043123, and undo its reformat

Adding a freshness_acknowledgement to three artifacts, I wrote

    lst[:] = [e for e in lst if e.get("path") != dep] + [ack]

which REPLACES every prior entry for that dependency instead of appending. It
destroyed 49 prior acknowledgements in outer_loop_arc_gateway_accurate_rescore,
28 in outer_loop_arc_gateway_rescore, and 1 in outer_loop_arc_max_actions_answer.
78 recorded review judgements, one of them a hand-written 2026-08-17 entry whose
prose evidence cited a specific commit range. That is a never-prune violation, and
I committed it.

Two things hid it. The damage was nested at provenance.freshness_acknowledgements,
and determination_preservation_lint checks top-level keys only -- a scope limit its
own docstring states and asks to widen only on a real nested incident. And I had
serialised with indent=2 where the originals use indent=1, so the same commit
carried a 12,000-line whitespace rewrite that would have buried the deletions from
any human reader.

This commit rebuilds all three files FROM the pre-damage original rather than from
my rewrite, restores the original indent=1 and trailing newline, and appends only
the genuinely new entries. Verified per file: prior acknowledgements present, in
their original order, and every other key byte-identical after parsing. The diff
against dac8043123~1 is now +32 insertions and 0 deletions.

The cascade entry was also repinned. It had recorded the sha of the indent=2
version, which stopped matching once the file was restored.

Stale artifact count returns to its pre-change baseline of 12.

Filed in known-issues, not built: the narrow widening this incident justifies is to
protect a top-level provenance object's freshness_acknowledgements list only --
never all nested provenance, which the lint author correctly rejected as
cry-wolf, since per-row provenance is rewritten wholesale by honest re-runs. That
one path is never per-row, and legitimate rebuilds already preserve it through
preserve_freshness_acknowledgements(), so the guard would fire only where that
helper was skipped. Not implemented here: widening a guard needs a mutation proof
and a corpus A/B, and this was found immediately after the slip it describes.

Working rule recorded: when editing an acknowledgement or corrigendum list, APPEND;
never filter-and-replace; diff against the original and confirm zero deletions
before staging; never let a reformat share a commit with a content edit to an
evidence file.

